     1	"""Local container backend — the lowest-isolation tier (tool-sandbox-contract §5.1).
     2	
     3	The proven Docker/OCI backend (`GvisorSandboxService`) pointed at a LOCAL container
     4	socket with the standard `runc` runtime — no SSH, no remote host. The sandbox runs on
     5	the same machine as the app: the simplest deployment (a stranger cloning the repo on
     6	one Linux box) and the cross-platform target (Windows validation deferred).
     7	
     8	This is almost entirely a config variant of the Docker backend — same docker-py client,
     9	session model, exec/file-ops, capability sealing, never-pull, typed errors. The ONE
    10	behavioral difference is the workspace: a per-run NAMED VOLUME rather than a remote-
    11	daemon bind-mount. A named volume is portable across both local runtimes — rootless
    12	Podman (reached via its Docker-compatible socket) can't bind-mount an auto-created host
    13	path (the VM 202 lesson), and local Docker handles named volumes identically.
    14	
    15	Isolation here is container-grade only (SHARED host kernel) — weaker than gVisor. See
    16	`isolation.py`: this tier is honest about that and couples to a tighter confirmation
    17	default, so the weak sandbox is never silently as permissive as the strong tier.
